# Copy to .env.local for local runs. Vite only exposes vars prefixed with VITE_.

# Where the app finds the API. Set this to the API *origin* only — the path prefix `/api/v1` is
# already part of every request (see src/api/client.ts). Leave it unset to use the current origin,
# which is what the composed stack does: nginx serves the SPA and reverse-proxies /api on the same
# origin (docker-compose.e2e.yml / docker-compose.prod.yml), so no build-time URL is needed.
# Example for a separately hosted API during local dev:
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Enable the in-browser MSW mock backend for the dev server (off unless set). The E2E build sets
# this itself; you rarely need it here.
# VITE_ENABLE_MSW=true
